Lab Setup
Launch a terminal session
Verify NetworkManager is running:
sudo systemctl status NetworkManager
If not running, start it with:
sudo systemctl start NetworkManager
Task 1: Listing Network Devices with nmcli
Subtask 1.1: List all network devices
nmcli device status
Expected Output:
A table showing devices (eth0, wlan0, etc.), their type, state, and connection.

Subtask 1.2: Show detailed device information
nmcli device show
Key Concept:
This shows IP addresses, routes, DNS, and hardware details for all interfaces.

Task 2: Configuring Static IP Address
Subtask 2.1: Identify current connection name
nmcli connection show
Troubleshooting:
If no connections appear, check if interfaces are up with ip link.

Subtask 2.2: Add static IP configuration
sudo nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" \
ipv4.addresses 192.168.1.100/24 \
ipv4.gateway 192.168.1.1 \
ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8,8.8.4.4" \
ipv4.method manual
Explanation:

Sets static IP 192.168.1.100 with /24 subnet
Configures gateway and Google DNS servers
Changes method from DHCP to manual
Subtask 2.3: Apply changes
sudo nmcli connection up "Wired connection 1"
Task 3: Modifying Connection Profile
Subtask 3.1: View current profile settings
nmcli connection show "Wired connection 1"
Subtask 3.2: Change MTU size
sudo nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" 802-3-ethernet.mtu 1500
Subtask 3.3: Disable IPv6
sudo nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv6.method disabled
Task 4: Restarting NetworkManager
Subtask 4.1: Restart service
sudo systemctl restart NetworkManager
Subtask 4.2: Verify status
systemctl status NetworkManager
Expected Outcome:
Active (running) status with no errors

Task 5: Hostname and DNS Configuration
Subtask 5.1: Set hostname
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname mylabhost
Verify with:

hostnamectl
Subtask 5.2: Configure DNS resolution
Edit resolv.conf (temporary):

sudo nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.dns "1.1.1.1 1.0.0.1"
For permanent changes:

sudo nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.ignore-auto-dns yes
Verification Steps
Check IP configuration:

ip addr show
Test network connectivity:

ping -c 4 8.8.8.8
Verify DNS resolution:

nslookup google.com
Troubleshooting Tips
If changes don't apply:

Restart the interface: sudo nmcli device disconnect eth0 && sudo nmcli device connect eth0
For DNS issues:

Check /etc/resolv.conf contents
Test with dig example.com
Connection not appearing?

Rescan devices: sudo nmcli device reapply eth0
